WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.702
-You look gorgeous.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.970
-Thank you.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.872
-Thanks for playing
"Catchphrase."

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.474
I wanted to ask you --
I have a ton of questions.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.676
Because last time
I believe we talked,

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.445
we discussed an RV trip.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.914
-Oh, yeah, from New York to --

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.849
I sound so Canadian
all of a sudden.

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:18.785
-I know. You do.
-"Oh, yah! Oh, yah!

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.953
Oh, Gawd, yah! Oh, my Gawd."

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:23.122
-Soaree.
-"So soaree about that."

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:26.592
But, yes, we drove
from New York to Los Angeles.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:27.927
-Oh, that's right.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.629
-Yes.
-That's a major deal.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.230
-Those are both cities. Yes.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.800
-And was it as amazing
as you thought it would be?

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.570
-It was -- It was intense
'cause we did it in an RV

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.705
in, you know, 11 days.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:43.242
-So that was --
You know, we survived.

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:44.878
-[ Laughs ] "We survived."
-We survived.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.612
-Was -- Is it just
great memories, though?

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:47.880
Is it like --
-Yeah. It is --

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.582
It is, now, reflecting...

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.217
-Yeah.
-...back upon it.

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.286
But we're a big, like,
road-trip family.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:57.524
We drove up to Canada just
this past summer in August.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:58.824
-Wow.

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:02.295
-And that was...
also enjoyable.

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:05.531
-Wow. That was really --
You really tried to sell that.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:08.167
-You know, it -- it --
It's great. It's great.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.636
I mean, this is the time
to be doing road trips, right?

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:12.137
-Of course.
-This is the time.

00:01:12.137 --> 00:01:15.608
It's just that we decided to,
like, do 11 hours and 11 hours.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.810
Like, a 20-hour journey.
-No.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.778
And the kids are what age?

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:22.248
-They're 12 and 6.
-Yeah, okay, so that's --

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:24.083
-Yeah, young.
-Young, but still that's tough.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.785
12 is, like, okay --

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:27.887
-Yeah, it's like
that would be the age

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.755
that you'd be rocking
the Gameboy

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.324
if your parents
let you have a Gameboy.

00:01:32.324 --> 00:01:33.559
-Yeah.
-Which we don't.

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:35.394
-You don't have a Gameboy?
-No. No. No.

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.163
-What were you like
when you were 12?

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.598
-I -- Whoa. I was --

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:43.235
Gosh. So, so, so bad.

00:01:43.235 --> 00:01:44.904
-You were a bad kid?
-I was a bad kid.

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:48.741
And so it's really weird
having a child who's sort of

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:52.077
approaching that age of,
like, doing bad things

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:53.879
and, like, she's an angel.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:56.082
But I was like, you know --
I was really --

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.751
I was -- really cared about
what people thought about me.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.486
And I was really grungy,

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.989
and I was, like, super
into Aerosmith music videos.

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:05.658
-Yeah. Really?
-I mean, who wasn't?

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.859
Let's be honest.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.962
Alicia Silverstone
and Liv Tyler --

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.396
-The coolest kids in school.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.931
-Like, the coolest --
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.966
-The coolest freaking kids.
-That was so interesting.

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:15.802
They were in,
like, three videos.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.937
-I remember two.
It might have been more.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.373
But it was --
"Crazy" was both of them.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.208
And then "Crying" was this --

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.077
Sorry, "Cryin'".
It was an "N."

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:26.678
-"Cryin'". Oh, yeah.
-No "I-N-G." "Cryin'."

00:02:26.678 --> 00:02:29.882
-And Alicia Silverstone
was, like, the star of that,

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.618
and she got, like,
broken up with,

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:34.787
and then she went on this,
like, journey and met this guy,

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:37.723
and then he stole her purse,
and she karate kicked him.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.291
-Oh.
-It was wonderful.

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.726
And I loved it so --

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:45.130
I loved it so much that
I would, like, re-create it.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:49.369
-In your bedroom or something?
-No, in our basement.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:51.270
With a punching bag.
-Wow.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:55.274
-'Cause I thought that that
move, that kick was so cool.

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:58.244
And I did it and I kicked it,

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.012
and I fell and I broke my elbow.

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:01.814
-[ Audience awws ]
-She's okay.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.316
-Thank you.
-She's okay.

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:04.884
-No. Everyone was like, "Aww."

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:08.320
-And it was --
This is, like, end of summer,

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:10.156
going back
into the seventh grade,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.957
which is a big deal in Canada,

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:14.660
'cause you're, like, last year
of elementary school,

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.562
so you're like top dog.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.397
And I was like,
"I cannot go to school

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.900
with a -- with a cast on."
-No. Of course not.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.135
-I refused.
-Yeah.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.237
-So my plan was...

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:27.640
I was not going to
tell my mother anything.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.542
And I was just going to hide it.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.210
And I got through it
for a couple of hours,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.612
and then as soon
as she came home,

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.480
I was like -- [Sobbing]
"Mommy, I hurt myself."

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.849
-[ Laughter ]
-"I think I'm really hurt."

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.551
-See? Mom was there
for you, right?

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.252
She was fine.
-She was fine.

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:42.688
And we got a cast.
And it was fine.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.958
I told everybody I hurt myself
skateboarding, to be cool.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.093
-Yeah. You weren't kicking
a punching bag

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:50.062
pretending you're
Alicia Silverstone.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.431
-No, I wasn't.
-No, of course not.

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:53.299
-No, I don't even know
what you're talking about.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.334
-Cobie, I told you this
backstage,

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.170
but I'll say it again
in front of everybody.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.373
"Impeachment."
I'm watching the show.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.141
I think Beanie was on the show.
-mm-hmm.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.409
-Who's amazing.
-Yes, yes.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:04.811
-Plays Monica Lewinsky.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.112
And it's about the Bill Clinton,

00:04:07.112 --> 00:04:08.480
Monica Lewinsky,
the whole scandal.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.815
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:12.719
-I'm watching it,
and Ann Coulter --

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.253
Someone's playing Ann Coulter
on the show.

00:04:14.253 --> 00:04:16.622
-Right.
-And I go, "She's phenomenal.

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:18.291
She's great." It's you.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:19.459
-It is, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.293
-Yes, that was me.
-And you're phenomenal,

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:23.296
but I didn't even know
that you were in this.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:24.430
And I go, "Wait. This is --"

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.099
I can't wait to talk to you
about this.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.300
-Yeah.
-You dove right in.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.867
This is unbelievable!
-I jumped in.

00:04:28.867 --> 00:04:30.536
I jumped in, blond wig and all.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.571
-Well, did you --
How did it work out?

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:34.907
When did you shoot this?
-Well, we shot it --

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.476
I shot my portion of it.
It's been a long-running series.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:39.812
People have been working
really, really hard on it,

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:42.815
but I jumped in
like January of this year.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:45.418
And I'm in about six episodes.

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:47.920
And it's been --
it's been super fun.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.388
-You crush it.
-Thank you.

00:04:49.388 --> 00:04:51.356
-How did you get the voice down
and everything?

00:04:51.356 --> 00:04:53.826
Did you, like, study?
-Yeah, I listened to --

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:55.761
She wrote a lot of books.
-Yeah, she did.

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:58.664
And I listened to a lot of them
'cause she read them out loud.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:05:03.002
So I listened to her voice,
and I --

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:04.403
There's a lot of interviews.

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:06.572
She does -- Girlfriend
likes to, like, interview.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.641
-Yes. Of course.
-She puts herself out there.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.042
-Yeah.

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.877
-And so she -- she likes
to put herself out there,

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:15.147
so you can watch a lot of
footage of her in those moments.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:17.116
-Is there a word or something
that gets you

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.084
into the character?
-There was a few.

00:05:19.084 --> 00:05:22.121
It sort of started with...

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.857
[As Coulter]
"American Republicans."

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.093
-"American."
-"The way --

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:29.896
She doesn't open her mouth
very wide.

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:33.165
And then it kind of
went to just a sound,

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:37.603
which would be like,
'Um, um. Um.'"

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:40.439
-Oh, my God. Wow.
-Yeah.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:44.143
Because I think
she is always in a position

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.146
where she thinks she's smarter
than everybody else, you know?

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:50.482
And so it's just, like,
"She can't -- No.

00:05:50.482 --> 00:05:51.917
Like, she just can't."

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:53.185
-"No. Just can't."
-"No."

00:05:53.185 --> 00:05:54.553
-I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:55.821
Here's Cobie Smulders

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:57.456
In "Impeachment:
American Crime Story."

00:05:57.456 --> 00:06:00.225
Take a look.
-You're boring.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:02.261
That's the problem
with you Republicans.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:05.364
-You're a Republican.
-Mnh. I'm a conservative.

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:06.766
You're all too nice.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:09.902
What does that get you?
It -- It gets you Dole.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:13.672
-What's wrong with Dole?
-Um...he lost?

00:06:13.672 --> 00:06:15.875
Idiotic American females
couldn't wait

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:18.010
to re-elect their fat boyfriend.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:22.115
-Be that as it may,
this case is all we have now.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:26.852
-Right.

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:29.388
What would you like me to do?

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:33.325
-What you do best. Stir the pot.

00:06:33.325 --> 00:06:35.761
-Uh, help us
get justice for Paula.

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:38.297
-Oh, this isn't about justice.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.198
-Then what is it about?

00:06:40.198 --> 00:06:42.701
-Impeachment, Jerome.

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:46.506
-There you go. Cobie Smulders.

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:49.208
"Impeachment:
American Crime Story"

00:06:49.208 --> 00:06:51.911
airs Tuesdays
at 10:00 p.m. on FX.

